Subject: AI_AB_TEST: a Worker in every strike list; Mongolia sized to about 4
 Horses (Personality)

trial29 (18B3086C, ab-03494ee), the lead and Economy: Mongolia's list item 6 (Chariot Archer) waited T29-T60. The capital
had Animal Husbandry by T22 and a Horse tile in its borders from T25, but no Worker until about T53, so the Pasture came
at T53. Mongolia's list had no Worker, nor had the Huns', Greece's or the Celts'. Each now has a Worker 3rd.

The user (2026-11-07): "horses arent that rare, but having 10 seems very unlikely". The Mongol row needed 10 Horses
(8 Chariot Archers + 2 Horsemen; an upgrade keeps its Horse). Now core Knight (Keshik) x4 from 4 pre-built Chariot
Archers, support Spearman x2 to capture, siege Catapult x1. The list follows fils' opening with a Worker 3rd, then Archers,
Spearmen and a Catapult after the 4 Chariot Archers. Research puts Animal Husbandry and The Wheel 2nd and 3rd, Mathematics
for the Catapult. Plan contents stay game-data only.

LEAD: for the next block, on ai/war ae8e9ae: a Worker 3rd in the Huns, Greece, Celts and Mongolia lists; Mongolia's row is 4 Keshiks (4 pre-built Chariot Archers), 2 Spearmen, 1 Catapult, Animal Husbandry 2nd. ai/personality, CI pending; War merges.

